{"title":"Topology","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Topology</b> is a field of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics\" title=\"Mathematics\">mathematics</a> that can be considered an extension to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">geometry</a>: It involves the study of space and its structure. The word \"topology\" also denotes a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Topological_space\" title=\"Topological space\">topological space</a>, a specific kind of mathematical construct that satisfies certain axioms.  Topology is often considered one of the cornerstones of pure mathematics.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Important_Concepts\">Important Concepts</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Topology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Important Concepts\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Homeomorphism\" title=\"Homeomorphism\">Homeomorphism</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diffeomorphism\" title=\"Diffeomorphism\">Diffeomorphism</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ambient_isotopy&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Ambient isotopy (page does not exist)\">Ambient isotopy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Manifold\" title=\"Manifold\">Manifold</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Topology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Graph_theory\" title=\"Graph theory\">Graph theory</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">Geometry</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Knot_theory\" title=\"Knot theory\">Knot theory</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dynamical_system&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Dynamical system (page does not exist)\">Dynamical system</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Klein_bottle&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Klein bottle (page does not exist)\">Klein bottle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Moebius_strip\" title=\"Moebius strip\">Moebius strip</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fractal\" title=\"Fractal\">Fractal</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Topology&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018112217\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 19/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 265/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.450      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.450      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6179:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018112217 and revision id 153867. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}